<title>USA: V-ONE IPO shares lowered, price range raised.</title>
<headline>V-ONE IPO shares lowered, price range raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>V-ONE Corp, previously known as Virtual Open Network Environment Corp, has slightly lowered the number of shares and raised the price range on its upcoming initial public offering, according to underwriter Piper Jaffray.</p>
<p>The number of shares has been cut to 3.3 million from 3.4 million, while the estimated price range has been revised upward to $6 to $8 per share from $5 to $6 per share.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to make its debut on the Nasdaq sometime in early or mid-October under the proposed stock symbol &quot;VONE.&quot;</p>
</text>
